Subject: [PATCH 33/37] s13d g4 cont4: the found path's time bound; the
 screen's new copies factored
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The found path runs in at most 1000 · 2^(i₀ + 1) + 200 steps: each round's time bounded by its
level, the passes' times by their geometric sums. The checkpoint's copy-text screen pairs at 90%
or more are factored through shared helpers (the never-halting exit sets, the pop rounds' and the
returns' escapes, the home tests, the peek branch, the field starts' monotonicity, a field's
first cell, the segment-built re-index, the one-cell branches' ways back, the room probe's box),
and the pinned branch takes a test that moves its pin.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0155fKrzMUhziJHzQxJacYbw
